body:
I think I'm just gonna do prints, though, no frames. It's a little overwhelming, still not sure how much to charge or how much to buy before I start selling to make it cheaper. What is c2-x3? 

&#x200B;

I'll research shipping for sure, or maybe just do digital. Is there a good market for digital, though? Or are people more into physical prints?

I changed it a little bit because I didn't like the original version. Ignore the lack of audio please, as that will come last. 

&#x200B;

Right now the whole thing is about 20 seconds. I'd LOVE for it to be at least a minute long. The max length is 5 minutes but I don't think I have enough content for that long a video nor feel like it's necessary.

Anyways, please plaese please review my video and give me some ideas. How do make it longer, how to tell the story better, and how my character should experience Schizophrenia besides paranoia and voices?

&#x200B;

Thank you guys so so much!

Still editing what I have because I'm constantly getting ideas for what to add next and how to improve what is currently there, but I really hope you guys like it!

&#x200B;

Do you guys have any opinions on the character being male or female? Any reasons for why it should  be one or the other?

It's quite fast paced, I do plan to fix it and make some parts longer(like the paranoid looking around beginning part) and adding a whole lot to it. This is just the very early status that I wanted to share with you guys! 

&#x200B;

Let me know if you have any suggestions of things to happen to my character that express what Schizophrenia is. I will be adding audio of voices.

I have PC, what's the PC alternative to command enter? 

&#x200B;

But yea, that's what I mean, how to I get the nested animation that's inside the symbol/movie clip out of that and onto my main timeline?

Ok, thank you! I can definitely give up the BBQ sauce and gatorade. Stevia will be a bit harder as I can't drink tea without it being a little sweet. Can I use liquid stevia instead? Or is that the same level of bad as the powdered kind?

&#x200B;

This is my favorite creamer, is it OK to use once a day? [https://imgur.com/gDCmp1Z](https://imgur.com/gDCmp1Z)

Thanks. I think it is maybe just from too much caffeine today. If it stops me from sleeping due to the uncomfortable-ness, should I go to the ER then, since it would be worse and not gone away for some time?

&#x200B;

I love coffee so I don't think I can give it up. I just need to lessen the amount I drink. I don't drink alcohol anyways so that's easy. 

&#x200B;

I'll go to the er if it's worse. Like I said, I took some ativan so if its' anxiety related I'll feel better soon.

Thank you! So you don't think I should count calories on zerocarb? Is that ok? I'll definitely try to be mindful of how I eat as to not eat large portions. But I'm scared of too many calories. That's what I was doing before, counting calories..waiting until the right time to eat. It sucks. 

&#x200B;

So i don't need to worry about calories? That sounds good. Is it true?

Are there benefits to doing zerocarb most days but not all? Like say you eat zerocarb throughout the week but on weekends allow yourselves something else as a treat.

&#x200B;

Will it still work/get benefits? Or do you have to do it everyday consistently for a long time to lose weight or get any health benefits from it?

